titanfall 2 is a game about momentum it  knows when to rush forward at a  breakneck pace it knows when to give us  time to breathe both in its  single-player campaign and its  multiplayer modes titanfall 2 is a more  measured pace than its predecessor  making the build-up to its climactic  battles just as enticing as the events  themselves it's every bit as kinetic and  fluid is the first titanfall but in many  respects it's a much better shooter as  with the first game from respawn  entertainment titanfall 2 revolves  around two layers of combat conventional  firefights between human combatants and  clashes between massive bipedal mechs as  a boots on the ground pilot titanfall 2  feels more like a traditional shooter  albeit one with pristine controls in a  fluid traversal system then it comes  time to call in your mechanical ally  from orbit and everything changes  because it's when these two layers  engage in a tug of war that titanfall 2  reveals its true brilliance what was  once an even fight becomes a David  versus Goliath scenario as a pilot  escapes the cover and calls in a Titan  of her own momentum often shifts like  this as one team gains control of the  battlefield only to lose ground when the  other notice is a weak spot  this is crucial in titanfall 2 now more  than ever  combat requires forethought and  intelligence despite the bombast and  spectacle titanfall 2 is a thinking  person shooter the sequels new Titans  embody the sentiment in place of the  basic light medium and heavy variants  from the first game titanfall 2 employs  six distinct walking battle tanks with  Arsenal's of their own they're almost  like superheroes one attacks with a  thermite launcher in flame weapons while  the other fires a chest mounted laser  cannon an unlucky opponents each of  these titans abilities are easy to learn  but difficult to master as the saying  goes their loadout to immediately make  sense but the more you play the more  emergent scenarios you'll find learning  the intricacies of each Titan is  paramount not just for offense but  defense to their elements of fighting  games or MOBAs here each Titan has a  tell and you only have a few brief  moments to counter it to your advantage  the new Titans also lend a very  different pace to multiplayer matches  while the first titanfall was always  cranked up to 11 so to speak with  smaller maps and cook  cutter tighten variants focused on  dealing damage titanfall 2 understands  the value of breathing room it doesn't  burn you out with an onslaught of  firefights its match you're focused on  exterior environments and are often on  the larger wider side giving you time to  plan out your attack based on your Titan  load outs each multiplayer mode  facilitates titanfall to interwove and  combat systems but also twist the  formula in creative ways bounty hunt is  my favorite you gain currency by killing  the enemy team and AI grunts that litter  the map and at the end of each wave  you're given the chance to deposit your  loot in banks the thing is the other  team is doing the same thing it's a  frantic game of cat and mouse that  increases in tension as the banks open  and players rush to gain points that  expert attention to pacing in momentum  carries over into titanfall 2  single-player mode as well  it follows Jack Cooper a militia  rifleman turned pilot and his sentient  Titan BT 72 74 as they battle the  interstellar manufacturing corporation  and the apex predator mercenary group  unfortunately the writing here is  lacking your main enemies are outlandish  villains and the plot ends abruptly  before it feels like it should and while  there is often humour and sentiment to  be found between Cooper and BT the jokes  become wrote when they focus too much on  the Titans inability to understand human  sayings and turns of phrase missing me  already  I was not shooting at you that would be  a violation of protocol three yeah never  mind yet in terms of design and pacing  the for our campaign is fantastic it  gradually increases in velocity and  scope coalescing in midair ship battles  frantic Titan charges and old-school  boss fights well now we're talking as  you progress through these missions  you'll unlock all of titanfall to's  Titan loadouts getting the ability to  swap between them on the fly this grants  the campaign a dynamism not entirely  present in multiplayer you can enter a  battlefield discern this situation and  choose a different Titan based on this  scenario all in the span of several  seconds  good work pilot your skills are greatly  improving titanfall 2 accomplishes  several things it introduces seemingly  minor changes to its multiplayer sphere  but results in more fluid pacing in a  more intelligent gameplay loop it adds a  single-player campaign that builds in  momentum with each mission culminating  in grandiose battles that make use of  both Titan and pilot combat and lastly  titanfall 2 demonstrates a vitality that  its predecessor couldn't wear as the  first titanfall kept up its breakneck  pace throughout the entirety of every  match titanfall 2 understands that  sometimes dialing things back for a few  moments can make the long run much more  enjoyable in many ways titanfall 2 feels  like the game respawn should have made  in 2013 it's a fantastic sequel it's a  fluid shooter it's a spectacular game  range 95 meters projectile mass 89  kilograms  trust me  you  [Music]
 

